Browser VM — third-party components
==================================

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the application code in this repository
(index.html, app/, tools/, tests/, docs/). It does not cover the vendored
components below, which keep their own licences.

1. v86 — x86 PC emulator and x86-to-wasm JIT, running in the browser
   Files:  assets/v86/libv86.js, assets/v86/v86.wasm, assets/v86/v86-fallback.wasm,
           assets/v86/v86.d.ts, assets/v86/LICENSE-v86.txt
   Author: Fabian Hemmer and contributors — https://github.com/copy/v86
   Licence: Simplified BSD (2-clause). See assets/v86/LICENSE-v86.txt.

1b. v86_64 (optional) — experimental 64-bit long-mode fork of v86
   Files:  assets/v86_64/libv86.js, assets/v86_64/v86.wasm, assets/v86_64/v86-fallback.wasm
           when the operator vendors them from https://github.com/portlandhodl/v86_64
   Licence: Simplified BSD (2-clause), same as v86. Not shipped in this git tree
           until those release assets are added.

2. SeaBIOS (BIOS rom)
   Files:  assets/v86/seabios.bin
   Licence: GNU LGPL v3. See assets/v86/COPYING.LESSER.
   Source:  https://github.com/copy/v86 (bios/seabios.bin, built from SeaBIOS)

3. VGA BIOS rom
   Files:  assets/v86/vgabios.bin
   Licence: GNU LGPL v3. See assets/v86/COPYING.LESSER.
   Source:  https://github.com/copy/v86 (bios/vgabios.bin)

4. Demo boot images
   Files:  assets/images/tiny-linux.iso, assets/images/freedos.img, assets/images/kolibri.img
   Source: https://github.com/copy/images (the v86 project's test images)
   Contents:
     tiny-linux.iso  — Linux built with Buildroot (GPL and other free licences,
                       sources available from https://buildroot.org/ and the
                       component projects)
     freedos.img     — FreeDOS 7.22 (GPL; source: https://www.freedos.org/)
     kolibri.img     — KolibriOS (GPL; source: https://kolibri.os/)
   These are unmodified redistributions of freely licensed operating systems.
   See assets/images/README.md for checksums.

5. Alpine Linux / Fluxbox / Dillo desktop
   Files: assets/images/alpine-browser/fs.json and rootfs/*.bin.zst
   Distribution: Alpine Linux 3.23 x86, prepared from signature-verified APKs.
   Licences: individual packages retain their GPL, LGPL, MIT, BSD and other
             licences; the application MIT licence does not relicense them.
   Provenance and exact package versions: assets/images/alpine-browser/manifest.json
   Package sources, Alpine build recipes/patches and licence notices:
     https://github.com/rerebankole-glitch/VM/releases/download/alpine-browser-sources-38149903453-1/alpine-browser-sources.tar.zst
   GPL/LGPL texts are accessible inside the guest in /opt/webvm/licenses/.
   Current WebVM-owned guest configuration: tools/linux-browser/guest/.
   See docs/LINUX-BROWSER.md for source, build, checksums and resource limits.

Other catalogue ISO distributions (MX Linux, Ubuntu/Lubuntu, Linux Mint,
Debian, antiX, stock Alpine, Tiny Core, Arch Linux 32) are linked to their
upstream download locations, not bundled with this repository.
